  "pr": {
    "number": 82,
    "title": "fix(auth): sign-in/password-change race, change-password throttle, reviewer resets (AUD4-F06, F04, F02)",
    "state": "open",
    "draft": true,
    "mergeable": true,
    "mergeable_state": "unstable",
    "base": "main",
    "base_sha": "a62071d2c4e65027f4918c90d63e804b1deceb60",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-18T08:10:02Z",
    "body": "Fixes three findings from the 2026-11-18 ledger/authorization audit of `main`. Details: `docs/audit/consolidation-completion-2026-11/AUD4-AUTH-FIXES.md`.\n\n**AUD4-F06 (Medium, CWE-367): sign-in racing a password change.** `LoginStep` checked the password with Argon2 outside any write unit, then created the session without re-reading the hash. A password change, recovery or reset that committed in between revoked all sessions, but this sign-in then got a fresh session for the old password. That breaks SEC-003.\n- The unit that creates the session now re-reads the person and hash, and refuses if either changed.\n- `ChangePassword` overwrites only the hash it verified (compare-and-swap).\n- `ChangePassword` now also deletes pending second-factor challenges (SA2-13), as recovery and resets already do.\n\n**AUD4-F04 (Low, CWE-307): change-password guesses not durably throttled.** Guesses of the current password through a stolen session were limited only by the API's in-memory 5-per-minute limit. They now count against the durable `recgen` throttle, shared with the other re-authentication checks (A3-03). A successful change clears the counter.\n\n**AUD4-F02 (Medium, CWE-284): administrator can take over a reviewer.** An administrator who is a party to a dispute could reset the password of a reviewer without a second factor, sign in as that reviewer, and decide the dispute. Like administrators (SA2-01), reviewers can now only be reset by the platform operator, which preserves reviewer independence (DOM-038). Ordinary members are unchanged. **Owner note:** this is the conservative, reversible choice. Requiring a second factor for reviewers is an alternative.\n\nNew tests, in `internal/service/aud4_auth_test.go`:\n- `TestLoginStraddlingPasswordChangeGetsNoSession` (self-service change and administrator reset, made deterministic through the `ObserveArgon2` seam)\n- `TestChangePasswordReplacesOnlyTheVerifiedHash`\n- `TestChangePasswordGuessesAreThrottled`\n- `TestAdminCannotResetReviewerPassword`\n\nWith `auth.go` and `recovery.go` reverted, all four fail; with the fix, all four pass. golangci-lint v2.15.0 reports 0 issues and `go test ./...` passes. The `-race` run with a 40-minute timeout is still running after merging `main`; this PR's CI also runs it.\n\nNot fixed here, owner decisions recorded in the note: AUD4-F01 (dual-control check only covers one direction of the appointment chain; accepted as a side effect in the SEC-011 appendix), AUD4-F07 (sessions are not rotated on role change; no practical effect) and A3-F02 / DEC-014. AUD4-F03 (dispute timelines shortened retroactively) is handled in a separate PR.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01KtKj8n2B7N1ZkoQQdz85gS)_"
